I believe the swapper is to be ignored (https://lkml.org/lkml/2009/6/25/166)
but that still leaves xfsaild and rcu_sched

My suspects at the moment are:
 - the hrtimer issue reported on
https://bugzilla.kernel.org/show_bug.cgi?id=3D14424
 - the xfs issues reported before (
http://marc.info/?l=3Dlinux-xfs&m=3D134088105208917&w=3D2) but the patch ha=
s been
included in 3.14.25. I might move everything into a ext4 filesystem if that
can help.
 - some westmere related issues (http://lwn.net/Articles/479814/: Extend
mwait idle to optimize away IPIs when possible) but there is no more
idle=3Dmwait

